exports[`Part B: per-check trigger scenarios underscoreFormat — fires its check, output unchanged 1`] = `
[
  {
    "context": "preprocessor",
    "hint": "The erroneous value is:  <code class="alert-value">English</code> [column B]. <br><br>This may not be your fault, as the definition of “_language” changed on July 19, 2026. It used to accept only a language name, like “English”, and now it only accepts a BCP-47 language code, like “en”.<br><br>• If you provided a language name, please change it to a language code. Some popular ones are: Arabic ar, Chinese (Simplified) zh-Hans, Chinese (Traditional) zh-Hant, English en, French fr, Hebrew he, Hindi hi, Italian it, Japanese ja, Persian fa, Russian, ru, Spanish es. Look up “_language” in the Glossary to see the 42 language codes currently supported.<br><br>• If you provided a legal BCP-47 code not yet supported by EasyEyes, ask us to add it: denis.pelli@nyu.edu SUBJECT:EasyEyes.<br>",
